---
// Privacy Policy. Content is grounded in what the site actually does:
// free-review form + build/checkout → Netlify Blobs, Stripe Checkout for
// payments, Resend for operator notifications. No analytics/ad trackers.
import LegalPage from "../components/LegalPage.astro";
import { legal, subProcessors } from "../lib/legal.mjs";
---
<LegalPage
  title="Privacy Policy — Better Business Web"
  description="How Better Business Web collects, uses, and protects your information."
  heading="Privacy Policy"
>
  <p>
    This policy explains what information {legal.businessName} ({legal.entityDescription})
    collects when you use this website ({legal.domain}), how we use it, and the
    choices you have. We keep it short and in plain English.
  </p>
  <p>
    This policy covers <strong>our own website</strong>. Websites we design and
    build for clients are separate and are covered by each client's own privacy
    policy.
  </p>

  <h2>Information you give us</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Free website review or preview.</strong> When you submit the
      review form, we collect your name, your email or phone number, and the
      details you choose to share — business name, city and state, your current
      website (or "none"), and what you're looking for.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Orders.</strong> When you buy a bundle, we collect your business
      name, your contact email or phone, and the services you select.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Payment information</h2>
  <p>
    Payments are processed by <strong>Stripe</strong>. Your card details are
    entered on Stripe's secure checkout and go directly to Stripe — we never
    receive or store full card numbers. We receive limited information from
    Stripe needed to fulfil and manage your order, such as confirmation that a
    payment succeeded, your billing contact, and your subscription status.
  </p>

  <h2>Information collected automatically</h2>
  <p>
    This site does <strong>not</strong> use advertising or analytics trackers,
    and we don't build profiles of you across the web. To serve the site and
    keep it secure, our host (Netlify) processes standard request logs, which
    include your IP address. We also use your IP address briefly to rate-limit
    the checkout form against abuse. See our <a href="/cookies">Cookie Policy</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>How we use your information</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>To prepare your website review or preview and get back to you.</li>
    <li>To provide, set up, and bill for the services you order.</li>
    <li>To respond to your questions and provide support.</li>
    <li>To prevent fraud and abuse of our forms and checkout.</li>
    <li>To meet our legal and accounting obligations.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    We will only use your details for the reasons above. We don't send spam, and
    we won't share your information for anyone else's marketing.
  </p>

  <h2>Who we share it with</h2>
  <p>
    We don't sell your personal information. We share it only with the service
    providers that help us run the business, and only as needed:
  </p>
  <ul>
    {subProcessors.map((p) => (
      <li>
        <strong>{p.name}.</strong> {p.role}{" "}
        <a href={p.url} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Privacy policy</a>.
      </li>
    ))}
  </ul>
  <p>
    When you hire us to set up tools on your behalf — such as a Google Business
    Profile, business email, a booking platform, or advertising — those run
    under your own accounts and are governed by those providers' terms and
    privacy policies. We may also disclose information if required by law.
  </p>

  <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
  <p>
    We keep review and order records for as long as needed to respond to you,
    deliver and support your services, and meet legal or accounting
    requirements. You can ask us to delete information we no longer need to keep.
  </p>

  <h2>Your rights and choices</h2>
  <p>
    You can ask us to access, correct, or delete the personal information we hold
    about you, and you can opt out of any emails. Depending on where you live
    (for example, under GDPR in the UK/EU or the CCPA in California), you may have
    additional rights — including the right to a copy of your data and, in
    California, to know that <strong>we do not sell or "share" personal
    information</strong> for cross-context behavioural advertising. To exercise
    any of these, email us at
    <a href={`mailto:${legal.contactEmail}`}>{legal.contactEmail}</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Security</h2>
  <p>
    We take reasonable measures to protect your information, including processing
    payments through Stripe and applying spam and rate-limiting protections on
    our forms. No method of transmission or storage is ever 100% secure, but we
    work to keep your data safe.
  </p>

  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>
    This site is meant for businesses and is not directed to children under 16.
    We don't knowingly collect information from children.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>
    We may update this policy from time to time. When we do, we'll change the
    "last updated" date at the top of this page.
  </p>
</LegalPage>
